/-!
# Ascent and descent of dualizing complexes along a syntomic base change

Let `φ : A → B` be a homomorphism of Noetherian rings which is syntomic and surjective on
spectra, or faithfully flat and a local complete intersection, or faithfully flat of finite type
with Gorenstein fibres.  Then `K` in `D(A)` is a dualizing complex for `A` exactly when
`K ⊗_A^L B` is a dualizing complex for `B`.

## Main results

* `Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_derivedExtensionScalars_of_upperShriek` — the ascent argument,
  from the invertibility of `ω^•_{B/A}` and the tensor formula at `K`.
* `Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_syntomic`,
  `Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_faithfullyFlat_lci` and
  `Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_gorensteinFibres` — the three
  cases of [Stacks, Tag 0E4D] at a polynomial presentation `p`, taking the inputs of the ascent
  direction that are not yet derived here as hypotheses at the single object `K`.

These are not the statements of record of Tag 0E4D.  Every input they take is proved in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.DualizingComplexes.SyntomicBaseChangeUnconditional`, which
states the three cases under exactly the source's hypotheses and with nothing carried, as
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_syntomic_unconditional`,
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_faithfullyFlat_lci_unconditional`
and `Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_gorensteinFibres_unconditional`.
The forms here are kept because a consumer holding the inputs for its own reasons — as the
scheme-level [Stacks, Tag 0E4N] does, quantified over affine pairs — can use them without
establishing the hypotheses of a case.

## Implementation notes

The descent direction is unconditional: it is [Stacks, Tag 0E4A], here
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_of_faithfullyFlat`, and the faithful flatness it needs is derived
from the hypotheses of each case — in case (1) from syntomicity together with surjectivity on
spectra, by [Stacks, Tag 00HQ].

The ascent direction is the source's argument: upper shriek of `K` is a dualizing complex by
[Stacks, Tag 0BZL], it differs from `K ⊗_A^L B` by the invertible twist `ω^•_{B/A} = φ^!(A)`,
and tensoring with an invertible object neither creates nor destroys the property of being
dualizing, which is `Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_tensor_of_isInvertible` and, in the direction
needed here, `Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_of_tensor_isInvertible` below.

Two inputs of that argument are taken as hypotheses in this file, at the single object `K` of
the statement rather than as natural isomorphisms.

* `hInv`, the invertibility of `ω^•_{B/A}`, is [Stacks, Tag 0E4B] for cases (1) and (2).  In
  case (3) `hInv` is *not* a hypothesis: it is derived from the Gorenstein fibres by
  [Stacks, Tag 0E4C], `Dualizing.isGorensteinRing_fiber_iff_isInvertible_upperShriekFunctor_unit`,
  which holds with nothing carried.
* `hTensor`, the identification `φ^!(K) = (K ⊗_A^L B) ⊗_B ω^•_{B/A}`, is the tensor formula of
  [Stacks, Tag 0BZU] composed with the change-of-rings projection
  `K ⊗_A^L ω = (K ⊗_A^L B) ⊗_B ω` of [Stacks, Tag 06Y6], the `changeOfRings` field of
  `CochainComplex.DerivedTensor.DerivedTensorChangeOfRings`.  Tag 0BZU's conclusion is stated
  for `Dualizing.derivedTensorProductOver`, so the composite needs the comparison of that
  functor with derived extension of scalars followed by derived tensoring, which is the
  left-derived-functor uniqueness of two further functors.

Neither input is open.  `hInv` is `Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation`'s
`isInvertible_upperShriekFunctor_obj_unit_of_isLocalCompleteIntersection`,
proved unconditionally in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.UpperShriek.CompleteIntersection` by the local criterion of
[Stacks, Tag 0FNT] — not only for a presentation whose kernel is generated by a weakly regular
sequence, which is the narrower
`…isInvertible_upperShriekFunctor_obj_unit_of_isWeaklyRegular` in the same file.  Tag 0BZU holds
with the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0BZE] discharged, as
`Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.nonempty_upperShriekFunctor_iso_derivedTensorProduct` in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.UpperShriek.DerivedTensorUnconditional`, and the composite
with the Tag 06Y6 projection is assembled in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.DualizingComplexes.SyntomicBaseChangeUnconditional`.  That
module therefore restates cases (1) and (2) with nothing carried, as
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_syntomic_unconditional` and
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_faithfullyFlat_lci_unconditional`,
and case (3), whose only remaining input is `hTensor`, as
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_gorensteinFibres_unconditional`.

`Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex` here is the predicate over a *ring* of [Stacks, Tag 0A7B], the
structure declared in `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.Complex`; the development also has a
scheme-level predicate of the same short name,
`Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingComplex` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.RelativeDualizing.DualizingComplexScheme`, which is a
different notion and is not what any statement below is about.

Upper shriek depends on a presentation and is well defined only up to isomorphism, that
independence being [Stacks, Tag 0BZJ], which this library has unconditionally as
`Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.nonempty_upperShriekFunctor_iso`; as everywhere
else in this subtree the statements are nonetheless made at an arbitrary polynomial presentation
`p` of `φ`, which is the stronger reading and depends on Tag 0BZJ not at all.  A presentation
exists exactly when `φ` is of finite
type (`Dualizing.nonempty_polynomialPresentation`), so taking it as data also supplies the finite
type hypothesis of case (3).  The module universe is the universe of the two rings, which is the
generality of Tags 0BZL, 0BZU and 0E4C in this library.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E4D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E4D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E4A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E4A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E4B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E4B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E4C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E4C)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BZL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BZL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BZU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BZU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07D3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07D3)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory
open CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe u

namespace Dualizing

/-- **Cancelling an invertible tensor factor.**  If `X ⊗ L` is a dualizing complex for a
Noetherian ring and `L` is an invertible object of its derived category, then `X` is a dualizing
complex.  This is the converse reading of `Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_tensor_of_isInvertible`,
obtained by tensoring with a two-sided inverse of `L`. -/
theorem isDualizingComplex_of_tensor_isInvertible {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing B]
    {X L : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} B)}
    (hL : letI := (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      MonoidalCategory.IsInvertible L)
    (hXL : letI :=
        (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      IsDualizingComplex (X ⊗ L)) :
    IsDualizingComplex X := by
  let := (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
  obtain ⟨h⟩ := hL
  have hInv : MonoidalCategory.IsInvertible h.inv :=
    ⟨{ inv := L, isoLeft := h.isoRight, isoRight := h.isoLeft }⟩
  refine isDualizingComplex_of_iso ?_
    (isDualizingComplex_tensor_of_isInvertible hXL hInv)
  exact associator X L h.inv ≪≫ tensorIso (Iso.refl X) h.isoLeft ≪≫ rightUnitor X

section

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsNoetherianRing B]

/-- The relative dualizing complex `ω^•_{B/A} = φ^!(A)` read at a polynomial presentation `p` of
`φ : A →+* B`: the value of algebraic upper shriek at `A` placed in cohomological degree zero. -/
abbrev relativeDualizingUnit {f : A →+* B} (p : PolynomialPresentation f) :
    DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} B) :=
  p.upperShriekFunctor.{u, u}.obj
    ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of A A))

/-- **Ascent of a dualizing complex through an invertible twist of upper shriek.**  If `K` is a
dualizing complex for `A`, the relative dualizing complex `ω^•_{B/A} = φ^!(A)` of a presentation
`p` of `φ` is invertible, and `φ^!(K)` is `(K ⊗_A^L B) ⊗_B ω^•_{B/A}`, then `K ⊗_A^L B` is a
dualizing complex for `B`.

The three inputs are [Stacks, Tag 0BZL] for `φ^!(K)`, the invertibility hypothesis, and the
identification; the conclusion follows by cancelling the invertible factor. -/
theorem isDualizingComplex_derivedExtensionScalars_of_upperShriek
    (f : A →+* B) (p : PolynomialPresentation f)
    (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) (hK : IsDualizingComplex K)
    (hInv : letI := (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      MonoidalCategory.IsInvertible (relativeDualizingUnit p))
    (hTensor : letI :=
        (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      Nonempty (p.upperShriekFunctor.{u, u}.obj K ≅
        ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} f).functor.obj K) ⊗
          relativeDualizingUnit p)) :
    IsDualizingComplex ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} f).functor.obj K) := by
  let := (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
  exact isDualizingComplex_of_tensor_isInvertible hInv
    (isDualizingComplex_of_iso hTensor.some (p.upperShriekFunctor_isDualizingComplex K hK))

/-- Ascent through the invertible twist together with descent along a faithfully flat `f`. -/
private theorem isDualizingComplex_iff_of_faithfullyFlat_of_upperShriek
    (f : A →+* B) (hff : f.FaithfullyFlat) (p : PolynomialPresentation f)
    (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A))
    (hInv : letI := (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      MonoidalCategory.IsInvertible (relativeDualizingUnit p))
    (hTensor : letI :=
        (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      Nonempty (p.upperShriekFunctor.{u, u}.obj K ≅
        ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} f).functor.obj K) ⊗
          relativeDualizingUnit p)) :
    IsDualizingComplex K ↔
      IsDualizingComplex ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} f).functor.obj K) :=
  ⟨fun hK => isDualizingComplex_derivedExtensionScalars_of_upperShriek f p K hK hInv hTensor,
    fun hKB => isDualizingComplex_of_faithfullyFlat f hff K hKB⟩

/-- **Tag 0E4D, case (1), with the ascent inputs as hypotheses.**  Let `φ : A → B` be a syntomic
homomorphism of Noetherian rings which is surjective on spectra and let `p` be a polynomial
presentation of `φ`. Then `K` in `D(A)` is a dualizing complex for `A` if and only if
`K ⊗_A^L B` is a dualizing complex for `B`.

Syntomic is flat and a local complete intersection by [Stacks, Tag 07D3], and a flat
homomorphism surjective on spectra is faithfully flat by [Stacks, Tag 00HQ], which is what the
descent direction of [Stacks, Tag 0E4A] needs.  The ascent direction carries the two inputs
described in the module documentation; both are proved there, and
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_syntomic_unconditional` is this
statement with them discharged. -/
theorem isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_syntomic
    (f : A →+* B) (hsyn : letI := f.toAlgebra; Algebra.Syntomic A B)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (PrimeSpectrum.comap f))
    (p : PolynomialPresentation f) (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A))
    (hInv : letI := (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      MonoidalCategory.IsInvertible (relativeDualizingUnit p))
    (hTensor : letI :=
        (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      Nonempty (p.upperShriekFunctor.{u, u}.obj K ≅
        ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} f).functor.obj K) ⊗
          relativeDualizingUnit p)) :
    IsDualizingComplex K ↔
      IsDualizingComplex ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} f).functor.obj K) := by
  have hflat : f.Flat :=
    ((RingHom.syntomic_iff_flat_and_isLocalCompleteIntersection f).mp hsyn).1
  have hff : f.FaithfullyFlat := ((faithfullyFlat_tfae00HQ f hflat).out 2 1).mp hsurj
  exact isDualizingComplex_iff_of_faithfullyFlat_of_upperShriek f hff p K hInv hTensor

/-- **Tag 0E4D, case (2), with the ascent inputs as hypotheses.**  Let `φ : A → B` be a faithfully
flat local complete intersection homomorphism of Noetherian rings and let `p` be a polynomial
presentation of `φ`. Then `K` in `D(A)` is a dualizing complex for `A` if and only if
`K ⊗_A^L B` is a dualizing complex for `B`.

The local complete intersection hypothesis is what [Stacks, Tag 0E4B] consumes to produce the
invertibility of `ω^•_{B/A}`.  Here `hlci` is recorded rather than consumed and the invertibility
is carried as `hInv`, so that a consumer holding `hInv` for other reasons can apply this
statement; `hlci` does discharge it, and
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_faithfullyFlat_lci_unconditional`
is this statement with both inputs discharged from `hlci`. -/
theorem isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_faithfullyFlat_lci
    (f : A →+* B) (hff : f.FaithfullyFlat) (hlci : RingHom.IsLocalCompleteIntersection f)
    (p : PolynomialPresentation f) (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A))
    (hInv : letI := (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      MonoidalCategory.IsInvertible (relativeDualizingUnit p))
    (hTensor : letI :=
        (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      Nonempty (p.upperShriekFunctor.{u, u}.obj K ≅
        ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} f).functor.obj K) ⊗
          relativeDualizingUnit p)) :
    IsDualizingComplex K ↔
      IsDualizingComplex ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} f).functor.obj K) := by
  -- Recorded, not consumed: `hlci` is the input of Tag 0E4B, which supplies `hInv`.
  have _hlci : RingHom.IsLocalCompleteIntersection f := hlci
  exact isDualizingComplex_iff_of_faithfullyFlat_of_upperShriek f hff p K hInv hTensor

/-- **Tag 0E4D, case (3), with the tensor formula as a hypothesis.**  Let `A → B` be a faithfully
flat homomorphism of Noetherian rings admitting a polynomial presentation `p`, hence of finite
type, and assume every fibre `B ⊗_A κ(q)` is Gorenstein.  Then `K` in `D(A)` is a dualizing
complex for `A` if and only if `K ⊗_A^L B` is a dualizing complex for `B`.

Here the invertibility of `ω^•_{B/A}` is not a hypothesis: it comes from the Gorenstein fibres by
[Stacks, Tag 0E4C].  `hTensor` is carried only to assume less:
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_gorensteinFibres_unconditional` is
this statement with it discharged from the flatness contained in `hff`, and with the presentation
obtained from finite type rather than given. -/
theorem isDualizingComplex_iff_derivedExtensionScalars_of_gorensteinFibres
    [Algebra A B] (hff : (algebraMap A B).FaithfullyFlat)
    (p : PolynomialPresentation (algebraMap A B))
    (hGor : ∀ (q : Ideal A) [q.IsPrime],
      letI := isNoetherianRing_baseChange q.ResidueField p
      IsGorensteinRing (q.Fiber B))
    (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A))
    (hTensor : letI :=
        (DerivedCategory.Invertible.derivedCategory_symmetricMonoidalCategory B).choose
      Nonempty (p.upperShriekFunctor.{u, u}.obj K ≅
        ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} (algebraMap A B)).functor.obj K) ⊗
          relativeDualizingUnit p)) :
    IsDualizingComplex K ↔
      IsDualizingComplex
        ((derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} (algebraMap A B)).functor.obj K) := by
  let : Module.Flat A B := RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff.mp hff.flat
  have hInv := (isGorensteinRing_fiber_iff_isInvertible_upperShriekFunctor_unit p).mp hGor
  exact isDualizingComplex_iff_of_faithfullyFlat_of_upperShriek _ hff p K hInv hTensor

end

end Dualizing

end
